Sval: a private page's audio stream carries no page title

A MediaTrackGraph names its OS audio stream after its document's title,
and renames it when the title changes. PulseAudio and PipeWire list each
stream's name to every app, and volume controls show it. A private
document's graph leaves the stream unnamed.

diff --git a/dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp b/dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp
index 45fbad1f6e..a46353f363 100644
--- a/dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp
+++ b/dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp
@@ -1736,7 +1736,8 @@ static nsCString GetDocumentTitle(uint64_t aWindowID) {
     return title;
   }
   Document* doc = win->GetExtantDoc();
-  if (!doc) {
+  // Sval: the title names the OS audio stream, which other apps can list.
+  if (!doc || doc->IsInPrivateBrowsing()) {
     return title;
   }
   nsAutoString titleUTF16;
